    <footnotes>
        <footnote id="F1">Represents performance share units (&quot;PSUs&quot;) that vested based on the appreciation in the share price of Hamilton Insurance Group, Ltd. (the &quot;Company&quot;) relative to the share price established following the Company's initial public offering. The award provided for a maximum of 250,000 PSUs, with the number of PSUs vesting based on the percentage increase from the average closing share price over the 30-trading-day period following the initial public offering to the average closing share price over the 30-trading-day period ending on the vesting date. The maximum 250,000 PSUs would vest upon a 100% or greater increase in the Company's share price over the applicable measurement period.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F2">Includes restricted stock units.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F3">Represents shares withheld to satisfy tax obligations arising out of the vesting of the reporting person's  PSUs.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F4">Represents the closing price per share on November 9, 2026, used to determine the number of shares to be withheld by the issuer to satisfy tax withholding obligations.</footnote>
